#ROOM
Vnum     300
Name     A Cheap Hotel~
Sector   city~
Flags    nomob indoors safe hotel~
Desc     This old hotel looks to be relatively safe if not clean. The rates are
cheap anyways. The walls are made of a synthetic wood material and the
floor is covered in a dirty brown carpet. Behind an old fashioned desk is
an assortmant of keycards sealed behind a more modern energy shield.  

This would be a good place to rest for a while. You may quit and renter
the game from here.

The streets belong to a future The Hague: dense, international, heavily connected and unmistakably Earth-born.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    420
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction southeast~
ToRoom    301
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     301
Name     Before The Hague Interstellar Terminal~
Sector   city~
Desc     You stand at a street corner in The Hague Government Quarter (also known as Directorate
City). The enormous city covers almost all of the planet Earth. The
street is suspended high above the ground as is dwarfed on all sides by
massive skyscrapers. Looking over the high railing at the edge of the road
you can see other similar streets many stories bellow and several more up
above. All around the city is bustling with activity.

Terran Union transit signs share the streetscape with old European stonework and newer composite towers.
~
